## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical knowledge of per-tenant configuration via Docker Config, feature gating, and edge proxy routing in a multi-DC setup.

## Key Concepts
- Docker Config for per-tenant rules
- Feature flag gating in API
- Traefik TLS and docker-dca wiring
- Lightweight bootstrap and config reload

## Code Example
```javascript
// sample Express middleware for feature gate
const fs = require('fs');
let flags = {};
try { flags = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync('/config/feature-flags.json','utf8')); } catch(e) { flags = {}; }
function featureGate(req,res,next){
  const tenant = req.headers['x-tenant'];
  if(!tenant) return res.status(400).send('Missing X-Tenant');
  const enabled = flags[tenant] && flags[tenant].includes('new-feature');
  if(!enabled) return res.status(403).send('Forbidden');
  next();
}
app.get('/new-feature', featureGate, (req,res)=>{ res.send('New feature access granted'); });
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you hot-reload the flags without restarting the API?
- How would you test isolation across tenants when flags change?

## Why This Is Asked
Demonstrates practical secret lifecycle management in Docker Swarm, integrating Vault for automated rotation with zero-downtime upgrades and proper secret versioning.

## Key Concepts
- Swarm secrets versioning and dynamic reattachment
- Vault-based rotation triggers and secret provisioning
- Rolling updates with start-first strategy to avoid downtime
- Health checks to confirm new secrets are loaded before removing old ones
- Atomic secret updates using add-then-remove pattern

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-automation: rotate Vault-derived Swarm secrets
async function rotateSecrets(serviceName, vaultPath) {
  // Fetch new credentials from Vault
  const newCreds = await vault.read(vaultPath);

  // Create new Swarm secrets
  const newSecrets = await createSwarmSecrets(newCreds);

  // Update service with new secrets
  await updateService(serviceName, newSecrets);

  // Verify health before cleanup
  await verifyServiceHealth(serviceName);

  // Remove old secrets
  await cleanupOldSecrets(serviceName);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
To assess practical config rotation in Swarm and application reload behavior.

## Key Concepts
- Docker Config rotation with versioned configs
- Rolling updates with update-parallelism and update-delay for zero downtime
- Graceful reload semantics (SIGHUP or /reload endpoint)
- Update order start-first to ensure new containers start before old ones stop

## Code Example
```javascript
// Node.js reload handler
const fs = require('fs');
let flags = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync('/etc/flags.json','utf8'));
process.on('SIGHUP', () => {
  flags = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync('/etc/flags.json','utf8'));
  // apply flags to runtime features
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the zero-downtime rollout in a CI pipeline?
- What failure scenarios would prompt you to revert the config rotation?
- How would you handle config validation before rotation?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to combine TLS edge proxying with per-tenant feature gates loaded from a daemon-managed config source. It also checks bootstrap discipline in a two-DC setup.

## Key Concepts
- Docker Configs for runtime config
- TLS termination at Nginx edge proxy
- Per-tenant feature gates in a small API
- Simple bootstrap for tenants and flags

## Code Example
```javascript
const fs = require('fs');
const yaml = require('js-yaml');
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
let flags = {};
function loadFlags() {
  const txt = fs.readFileSync('/etc/feature-flags.yaml','utf8');
  flags = yaml.load(txt) || {};
}
loadFlags();
app.get('/health-quiz', (req, res) => {
  const tenant = req.headers['x-tenant-id'];
  if (tenant && flags[tenant] && flags[tenant].enabled) res.sendStatus(200);
  else res.sendStatus(403);
});
app.listen(3000);
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test this gating with CI and two data centers?
- What are failure modes if the config-loader container is unavailable?
